---
description: General cursor rules for this project
---

- Repository/project provides an MCP server to access several Giant Swarm documentation sources
- Written in Go using version 1.25+
- Using Go modules for dependency management
- Main entry point is `cmd/server/main.go`
- Core implementation in `internal/search/` package
- `Dockerfile` provides multi-stage build for container image
- CHANGELOG.md should be updated for all changes
- Use `make build` to build the binary
- Use `make test` to run tests
- Use GitHub MCP tools to follow actions on GitHub PRs
- Use CircleCI MCP tools to follow build progress for PRs on CircleCI

## Documentation Structure

- `README.md` - User-facing documentation (installation, usage, quick start)
- `docs/` - Developer/technical documentation
  - `docs/architecture.md` - Technical architecture and design
  - `docs/security.md` - Security considerations
  - `docs/development.md` - Development setup and guidelines

## Search backend

- The search function at https://docs.giantswarm.io/searchapi/ is provided by OpenSearch v3.2
- Uses public endpoint (no authentication required in current version)
- Elasticsearch query structure uses v6.8.x query DSL with `function_score` and `simple_query_string`
- Field weights: `title^5`, `uri^5`, `description^5`, `text`
- Results include highlights and excerpts

## Authentication

- Authentication has been removed in the Go rewrite
- Will be reimplemented differently in a future version
- Currently only accesses public documentation endpoints
